# Device Detail Sheet

::summary
The device capability sheet (F-12), opened from This Workspace device rows — three capability rows where UNAVAILABLE rows state the reason per the parity honesty canon (shown with reason, never hidden): Browse files (read-only over the server relay — NOT desktop-only), Use for Surfy (routing toggle), Run build (explained-unavailable when the machine advertises no build cap). Remove device is the danger row.
::

::modal[name=device-detail title="mbp" width=340 placement=centered dismissible=true]

:::row[icon=folder action=browseDeviceFiles href=# trailing-label="Browse" trailing-action=browseDeviceFiles]
Browse files
Read-only, relayed through the server — nothing runs on the device
:::

:::row[icon=sparkle action=toggleUseForSurfy href=# trailing-label="On" trailing-action=toggleUseForSurfy]
Use for Surfy
Routing toggle — this device serves Surfy inference
:::

:::row[icon=task state=unavailable href=#]
Run build
Unavailable — this machine advertises no build capability
:::

:::row[icon=device style=danger action=removeDevice href=#]
Remove device
Revokes the device-scoped key; danger row, always last
:::

::

Top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. The title carries the device name; the same sheet serves every enrolled device, with capability rows reflecting what each machine advertises (mini would show Run build available as the deploy worker). Browse files opens `modals/device-files.surf`.

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
